.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Tina Smith (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Minnesota's open Senate seat features Democrat Peggy Flanagan against Republican Michele Tafoya after Tina Smith's retirement. The state leans Democratic by about three points, and Flanagan has out-raised Tafoya, though outside groups have spent heavily against her. Recent polls from late September show a remarkably tight contest, with several surveys putting Flanagan up only one or two points.\n\nDespite the tight polling, prediction markets still price Flanagan around 90% to win, and most expert raters place the race at Likely Democratic, with a couple at Lean Democratic. The forecast lands at a modest Democratic edge of roughly four to five points with above-average uncertainty, reflecting the gap between the tight polls and the more confident market and rater consensus.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8725, "margin": 5.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7776, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8131, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8217, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7867, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.784, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7719, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7956, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7935, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7758, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8073, "margin": 4.5}]}